From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Google's AMD DRI driver from /usr/lib64/cros/dri, loaded RTLD_LOCAL

minigbm's amdgpu backend allocates through Mesa's DRI driver interface
(radeonsi_dri.so). NickelOS Unified's Mesa is Gentoo's 26, whose
dri/radeonsi_dri.so is only the stub that loads libgallium and no longer
offers that interface: Google's driver (Mesa 24, LLVM inside) is kept for
minigbm alone in /usr/lib64/cros/dri, linked -Bsymbolic
(nickel-mesa-apart.bashrc) so its calls to what it defines itself
(amdgpu_winsys_create) don't land in Gentoo's libgallium, which exports
the same names. It loads RTLD_LOCAL now, so none of its symbols become
everyone's either: Gentoo's Mesa in the same process (Chrome's EGL) keeps
its own. Not RTLD_DEEPBIND: that binds the driver's free() to glibc's
under Chrome's own allocator ("double free or corruption" in the GPU
process, the AMD test PC, 2026-10-20).
---
--- a/dri.c	2026-09-30 22:56:30.217182346 +0000
+++ b/dri.c	2026-10-20 23:20:51.348081656 +0000
@@ -173,7 +173,12 @@
 
 void *dri_dlopen(const char *dri_so_path)
 {
-	return dlopen(dri_so_path, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_GLOBAL);
+	/*
+	 * NickelOS: loaded RTLD_LOCAL, so the driver's symbols stay its own:
+	 * on AMD it is Google's radeonsi, beside Gentoo's Mesa, whose
+	 * libgallium exports names it does too (DRI_PATH in amdgpu.c).
+	 */
+	return dlopen(dri_so_path, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL);
 }
 
 void dri_dlclose(void *dri_so_handle)
--- a/amdgpu.c	2026-09-30 22:56:30.209182373 +0000
+++ b/amdgpu.c	2026-10-20 23:20:51.348081656 +0000
@@ -25,7 +25,13 @@
 #include "util.h"
 
 // clang-format off
-#define DRI_PATH STRINGIZE(DRI_DRIVER_DIR/radeonsi_dri.so)
+/*
+ * NickelOS: Google's radeonsi DRI driver, kept for minigbm alone in
+ * /usr/lib64/cros/dri (nickel-unify) and linked -Bsymbolic: /usr/lib64/dri
+ * has Gentoo's Mesa's, which no longer offers the DRI interface minigbm
+ * calls.
+ */
+#define DRI_PATH "/usr/lib64/cros/dri/radeonsi_dri.so"
 // clang-format on
 
 #define TILE_TYPE_LINEAR 0
